cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "jaxgsa: Global Sensitivity Analysis in JAX"
abstract: >-
  jaxgsa computes global sensitivity indices entirely in JAX. It provides
  thirteen methods, covering variance-based indices (Sobol, eFAST, Kucherenko),
  screening (Morris, DGSM), moment-independent and given-data measures
  (Borgonovo delta, PAWN, HSIC, optimal transport), and surrogate-based
  analysis (PCE, RS-HDMR, Shapley effects, VKOGA). Eleven of the thirteen
  methods export a traceable core that runs under jit, vmap and grad, on CPU,
  GPU or TPU. Kucherenko and VKOGA are host NumPy and SciPy by design.
type: software
